3.7:
Arise, O Yahweh; save me, O my God!
For You have struck all my enemies on the cheek;
You have shattered the teeth of the wicked.

4.1:
Answer me when I call, O God of my righteousness!
You have relieved me in my distress;
Be gracious to me and hear my prayer.

5.9:
There is nothing reliable in their mouth;
Their inward part is destruction itself.
Their throat is an open grave;
They flatter with their tongue.

6.6:
I am weary with my sighing;
Every night I make my bed swim,
I flood my couch with my tears.

7.5:
Let the enemy pursue my soul and overtake it;
And let him trample my life down to the ground
And cause my glory to dwell in the dust. Selah.

7.6:
Arise, O Yahweh, in Your anger;
Lift up Yourself against the fury of my adversaries,
And arouse Yourself for me; You have appointed judgment.

9.6:
The enemy has come to an end in perpetual ruins,
And You have uprooted the cities;
The very memory of them has perished.

9.13:
Be gracious to me, O Yahweh;
See my affliction from those who hate me,
You who lift me up from the gates of death,

9.16:
Yahweh has made Himself known;
He has executed judgment.
In the work of his own hands the wicked is snared. Higgaion Selah.

10.5:
His ways prosper at all times;
Your judgments are on high, out of his sight;
As for all his adversaries, he snorts at them.

10.8:
He sits in the places of the villages where one lies in wait;
In the hiding places he kills the innocent;
His eyes stealthily watch for the unfortunate.

10.9:
He lies in wait in a hiding place as a lion in his lair;
He lies in wait to catch the afflicted;
He catches the afflicted when he draws him into his net.

10.14:
You have seen it, for You have beheld mischief and vexation to take it into Your hand.
The unfortunate commits himself to You;
You have been the helper of the orphan.

14.1:
The wicked fool says in his heart, “There is no God.”
They act corruptly, they commit abominable deeds;
There is no one who does good.

15.3:
He does not slander with his tongue,
Nor does evil to his neighbor,
Nor takes up a reproach against his friend;

15.4:
In whose eyes a reprobate is despised,
But who honors those who fear Yahweh;
He swears to his own hurt and does not change;

16.4:
The pains of those who have bartered for another god will be multiplied;
I shall not pour out their drink offerings of blood,
Nor will I take their names upon my lips.

16.11:
You will make known to me the path of life;
In Your presence is fullness of joy;
In Your right hand there are pleasures forever.

17.3:
You have tested my heart;
You have visited me by night;
You have tried me and You find nothing;
I have purposed that my mouth will not transgress.

18.2:
Yahweh is my rock and my fortress and my deliverer,
My God, my rock, in whom I take refuge;
My shield and the horn of my salvation, my stronghold.

18.7:
Then the earth shook and quaked;
And the foundations of the mountains were trembling
And were shaken, because He was angry.

18.8:
Smoke went up out of His nostrils,
And fire from His mouth devoured;
Coals were kindled by it.

18.30:
As for God, His way is blameless;
The word of Yahweh is tried;
He is a shield to all who take refuge in Him.

18.35:
You have also given me the shield of Your salvation,
And Your right hand upholds me;
And Your gentleness makes me great.

18.43:
You have delivered me from the contentions of the people;
You have placed me as head of the nations;
A people whom I have not known serve me.

18.48:
Who delivers me from my enemies;
Surely You lift me above those who rise up against me;
You rescue me from the violent man.

19.6:
Its rising is from one end of the heavens,
And its circuit to the other end of them;
And there is nothing hidden from its heat.

19.13:
Also keep back Your slave from presumptuous sins;
Let them not rule over me;
Then I will be blameless,
And I shall be acquitted of great transgression.

20.6:
Now I know that Yahweh saves His anointed;
He will answer him from His holy heaven
With the saving might of His right hand.

21.9:
You will make them as a fiery oven in the time of your anger;
Yahweh will swallow them up in His wrath,
And fire will devour them.

22.14:
I am poured out like water,
And all my bones are out of joint;
My heart is like wax;
It is melted within me.

22.15:
My strength is dried up like a potsherd,
And my tongue cleaves to my jaws;
And You lay me in the dust of death.

22.16:
For dogs have surrounded me;
A band of evildoers has encompassed me;
They pierced my hands and my feet.

22.23:
You who fear Yahweh, praise Him;
All you seed of Jacob, glorify Him,
And stand in awe of Him, all you seed of Israel.

22.24:
For He has not despised and He has not abhorred the affliction of the afflicted;
And He has not hidden His face from him;
But when he cried to Him for help, He heard.

22.26:
The afflicted will eat and be satisfied;
Those who seek Him will praise Yahweh.
May your heart live forever!

23.3:
He restores my soul;
He guides me in the paths of righteousness
For His name’s sake.

23.4:
Even though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death,
I fear no evil, for You are with me;
Your rod and Your staff, they comfort me.

23.5:
You prepare a table before me in the presence of my enemies;
You have anointed my head with oil;
My cup overflows.

25.2:
O my God, in You I trust,
Do not let me be ashamed;
Do not let my enemies exult over me.

25.5:
Lead me in Your truth and teach me,
For You are the God of my salvation;
In You I hope all the day.

25.7:
Do not remember the sins of my youth or my transgressions;
According to Your lovingkindness remember me,
For the sake of Your goodness, O Yahweh.

27.1:
Yahweh is my light and my salvation;
Whom shall I fear?
Yahweh is the strong defense of my life;
Whom shall I dread?

27.5:
For in the day of calamity He will conceal me in His shelter;
In the secret place of His tent He will hide me;
He will lift me up on a rock.

27.6:
And now my head will be lifted up above my enemies around me,
And I will offer in His tent sacrifices with loud shouts of joy;
I will sing, and I will sing praises to Yahweh.

27.9:
Do not hide Your face from me,
Do not turn Your slave away in anger;
You have been my help;
Do not abandon me and do not forsake me,
O God of my salvation!

27.14:
Hope in Yahweh;
Be strong and let your heart take courage;
Hope in Yahweh.

28.4:
Give to them according to their work and according to the evil of their actions;
Give to them according to the deeds of their hands;
Return their dealings upon them.

28.7:
Yahweh is my strength and my shield;
My heart trusts in Him, and I am helped;
Therefore my heart exults,
And with my song I shall thank Him.

29.3:
The voice of Yahweh is upon the waters;
The God of glory thunders,
Yahweh is over many waters.

29.9:
The voice of Yahweh makes the deer to calve
And strips the forests bare;
And in His temple everything says, “Glory!”

31.1:
In You, O Yahweh, I have taken refuge;
Let me never be ashamed;
In Your righteousness protect me.

31.2:
Incline Your ear to me, deliver me quickly;
Be to me a rock of strength,
A fortress to save me.

31.7:
I will rejoice and be glad in Your lovingkindness,
Because You have seen my affliction;
You have known the troubles of my soul,

35.8:
Let destruction, which he does not know, come upon him,
And let the net, which he hid, catch him;
Let him fall into it in destruction.

35.13:
But as for me, when they were sick, my clothing was sackcloth;
I humbled my soul with fasting,
And my prayer kept returning to my bosom.

35.15:
But at my stumbling they were glad and gathered themselves together;
The smiters whom I did not know gathered together against me,
They tore at me and never were silent.

35.27:
Let them shout for joy and be glad, who delight in my righteousness;
And let them say continually, “Yahweh be magnified,
Who delights in the peace of His slave.”

36.4:
He devises wickedness upon his bed;
He sets himself on a path that is not good;
He does not despise evil.

36.6:
Your righteousness is like the mountains of God;
Your judgments are like a great deep.
O Yahweh, You save man and beast.

37.7:
Be still in Yahweh and wait patiently for Him;
Do not fret because of him who prospers in his way,
Because of the man who carries out schemes of wickedness.

37.20:
But the wicked will perish;
And the enemies of Yahweh will be like the glory of the pastures,
They vanish—in smoke they vanish away.

37.34:
Hope for Yahweh and keep His way,
And He will exalt you to inherit the land;
When the wicked are cut off, you will see it.

37.40:
Yahweh helps them and protects them;
He protects them from the wicked and saves them,
Because they take refuge in Him.

38.12:
Those who search for my life lay snares for me;
And those who seek to do me evil have threatened destruction,
And they meditate on deception all day long.

39.3:
My heart was hot within me,
While I meditated the fire was burning;
Then I spoke with my tongue:

39.4:
“Yahweh, cause me to know my end
And what is the extent of my days;
Let me know how transient I am.

39.5:
Behold, You have made my days as handbreadths,
And my lifetime as nothing before You;
Surely every man, even standing firm, is altogether vanity. Selah.

39.6:
Surely every man walks about as a shadow;
Surely they make an uproar in vain;
He piles up riches and does not know who will gather them.

39.11:
With reproofs You chasten a man for iniquity;
You consume as a moth what is precious to him;
Surely every man is vanity. Selah.

39.12:
“Hear my prayer, O Yahweh, and give ear to my cry for help;
Do not be silent at my tears;
For I am a sojourner with You,
A foreign resident like all my fathers.

40.3:
He put a new song in my mouth, a song of praise to our God;
Many will see and fear
And will trust in Yahweh.

40.6:
Sacrifice and meal offering You have not desired;
My ears You have opened;
Burnt offering and sin offering You have not required.

40.9:
I proclaim good news of righteousness in the great assembly;
Behold, I do not restrain my lips,
O Yahweh, You know.

40.10:
I do not conceal Your righteousness within my heart;
I speak of Your faithfulness and Your salvation;
I do not hide Your lovingkindness and Your truth from the great assembly.

40.12:
For evils beyond number have surrounded me;
My iniquities have overtaken me, so that I am not able to see;
They are more numerous than the hairs of my head,
And my heart has failed me.

40.16:
Let all who seek You rejoice and be glad in You;
Let those who love Your salvation say continually,
“Yahweh be magnified!”

41.2:
Yahweh will keep him and keep him alive,
And he shall be blessed upon the earth;
And do not give him over to the desire of his enemies.

41.6:
And when he comes to see me, he speaks worthlessness;
His heart gathers wickedness to itself;
When he goes outside, he speaks it.

42.6:
O my God, my soul is in despair within me;
Therefore I remember You from the land of the Jordan
And the peaks of Hermon, from Mount Mizar.

42.8:
By day, Yahweh will command His lovingkindness;
And by night, His song will be with me,
A prayer to the God of my life.

43.3:
Oh send out Your light and Your truth, let them lead me;
Let them bring me to Your holy mountain
And to Your dwelling places.

43.4:
Then I will go to the altar of God,
To God my exceeding joy;
And upon the lyre I shall praise You, O God, my God.

44.2:
You with Your own hand dispossessed the nations;
Then You planted them;
You afflicted the peoples,
Then You cast them out.

45.1:
My heart overflows with a good theme;
I address my verses to the King;
My tongue is the pen of a skillful scribe.

45.2:
You are fairer than the sons of men;
Grace is poured upon Your lips;
Therefore God has blessed You forever.

45.4:
And in Your majesty ride on victoriously,
For the cause of truth and meekness and righteousness;
Let Your right hand teach You awesome things.

45.5:
Your arrows are sharp;
The peoples fall under You;
Your arrows are in the heart of the King’s enemies.

45.7:
You have loved righteousness and hated wickedness;
Therefore God, Your God, has anointed You
With the oil of joy above Your companions.

45.14:
She will be led to the King in embroidered work;
The virgins, her companions who follow her,
Will be brought to You.

46.9:
He makes wars to cease to the end of the earth;
He breaks the bow and cuts up the spear;
He burns the chariots with fire.

47.9:
The nobles of the peoples have assembled themselves with the people of the God of Abraham,
For the shields of the earth belong to God;
He is highly exalted.

48.8:
As we have heard, so have we seen
In the city of Yahweh of hosts, in the city of our God;
God will establish her forever. Selah.

48.10:
As is Your name, O God,
So is Your praise to the ends of the earth;
Your right hand is full of righteousness.

48.13:
Consider her ramparts;
Go through her palaces,
That you may recount it to the next generation.

48.14:
For this is God,
Our God forever and ever;
He will guide us over death.

49.10:
For he sees that even wise men die;
The fool and the senseless alike perish
And leave their wealth to others.

49.11:
Their inner thought is that their houses are forever
And their dwelling places from generation to generation;
They have called their lands after their own names.

49.14:
As sheep they are appointed for Sheol;
Death will shepherd them;
And the upright shall have dominion over them in the morning,
And their form shall be for Sheol to consume,
Far away from his habitation.

50.3:
May our God come and not be silent;
Fire devours before Him,
And a storm whirls around Him.

50.7:
“Hear, O My people, and I will speak;
O Israel, I will testify against you;
I am God, your God.

50.21:
These things you have done and I kept silent;
You thought that I was just like you;
I will reprove you and state the case in order before your eyes.

50.23:
He who offers a sacrifice of thanksgiving glorifies Me;
And he who orders his way,
I shall show the salvation of God.”

51.19:
Then You will delight in righteous sacrifices,
In burnt offering and whole burnt offering;
Then young bulls will be offered on Your altar.

52.5:
But God will break you down forever;
He will snatch you up and tear you away from your tent,
And uproot you from the land of the living, Selah.

53.1:
The wicked fool says in his heart, “There is no God,”
They act corruptly, and commit abominable injustice;
There is no one who does good.

53.5:
There they were in great dread where no dread had been;
For God scattered the bones of him who encamped against you;
You put them to shame, because God had rejected them.

54.3:
For strangers have risen against me
And ruthless men have sought my life;
They have not set God before them. Selah.

55.15:
Let death come deceitfully upon them;
Let them go down alive to Sheol,
For evil is in their dwelling, in their midst.

55.23:
But You, O God, will bring them down to the pit of corruption;
Men of bloodshed and deceit will not live out half their days.
But I will trust in You.

56.8:
You have taken account of my wanderings;
Put my tears in Your bottle.
Are they not in Your book?

57.3:
He will send from heaven and save me;
He reproaches him who tramples upon me. Selah.
God will send His lovingkindness and His truth.

57.6:
They have set a net for my steps;
My soul is bowed down;
They dug a pit before me;
They themselves have fallen into the midst of it. Selah.

59.3:
For behold, they have lain in wait for my soul;
Fierce men launch an attack against me,
Not for my transgression nor for my sin, O Yahweh,

59.5:
You, O Yahweh God of hosts, the God of Israel,
Awake to punish all the nations;
Do not be gracious to any who are treacherous in iniquity. Selah.

59.7:
Behold, they pour forth speech with their mouth;
Swords are in their lips,
For, they say, “Who hears?”

59.11:
Do not slay them, or my people will forget;
Make them wander about by Your power, and bring them down,
O Lord, our shield.

59.13:
Destroy them in wrath, destroy them that they may be no more;
That men may know that God rules in Jacob
To the ends of the earth. Selah.

60.7:
Gilead is Mine, and Manasseh is Mine;
Ephraim also is the helmet of My head;
Judah is My scepter.

60.8:
Moab is My washbowl;
Over Edom I shall throw My shoe;
Make a loud shout, O Philistia, because of Me!”

62.4:
Surely they have counseled to thrust him down from his high position;
They find pleasure in falsehood;
They bless with their mouth,
But inwardly they curse. Selah.

62.8:
Trust in Him at all times, O people;
Pour out your heart before Him;
God is a refuge for us. Selah.

62.9:
Surely men of low degree are merely vanity and men of rank are a lie;
In the balances they go up;
They are together lighter than a breath of vanity.

62.10:
Do not trust in oppression
And do not put vain hope in robbery;
If riches increase, do not set your heart upon them.

62.11:
Once God has spoken;
Twice I have heard this:
That strength belongs to God;

63.1:
O God, You are my God; I shall seek You earnestly;
My soul thirsts for You, my flesh yearns for You,
In a dry and weary land without water.

63.11:
But the king will be glad in God;
Everyone who swears by Him will boast,
For the mouths of those who speak lies will be closed.

64.5:
They hold fast to themselves an evil purpose;
They talk of laying snares secretly;
They say, “Who can see them?”

64.6:
They searched out unrighteousness, saying,
“We have completed a diligent search”;
For the inward thought of a man and his heart are deep.

65.9:
You visit the earth and cause it to overflow;
You greatly enrich it;
The stream of God is full of water;
You establish their grain, for thus You establish the earth.

65.13:
The meadows are clothed with flocks
And the valleys are covered with grain;
They make a loud shout, indeed, they sing.

66.4:
All the earth will worship You,
And will sing praises to You;
They will sing praises to Your name.” Selah.

66.6:
He turned the sea into dry land;
They passed through the river on foot;
There let us be glad in Him!

66.7:
He rules by His might forever;
His eyes keep watch on the nations;
Let not the rebellious exalt themselves. Selah.

66.12:
You made men ride over our heads;
We went through fire and through water,
Yet You brought us out into a place of abundance.

66.15:
I shall offer to You burnt offerings of fat beasts,
With the smoke of rams;
I shall make an offering of bulls with male goats. Selah.

67.4:
Let the nations be glad and sing for joy;
For You will judge the peoples with uprightness
And lead the nations on the earth. Selah.

68.2:
As smoke is driven away, so drive them away;
As wax melts before the fire,
So let the wicked perish before God.

68.4:
Sing to God, sing praises to His name;
Lift up a song for Him who rides through the deserts,
Whose name is Yah, and exult before Him.

68.6:
God causes the lonely to inhabit a home;
He leads out the prisoners into prosperity,
Only the rebellious dwell in a parched land.

68.8:
The earth quaked;
The heavens also dripped rain at the presence of God;
Sinai itself quaked at the presence of God, the God of Israel.

68.18:
You have ascended on high, You have led captive Your captives;
You have received gifts among men,
Even among the rebellious also, that Yah—God—may dwell there.

68.34:
Ascribe strength to God;
His majesty is over Israel
And His strength is in the skies.

69.4:
Those who hate me without cause are more than the hairs of my head;
Those who would destroy me are powerful, being wrongfully my enemies;
What I did not steal, I then have to restore.

69.13:
But as for me, my prayer is to You, O Yahweh, at an acceptable time;
O God, in the abundance of Your lovingkindness,
Answer me with the truth of Your salvation.

70.5:
But I am afflicted and needy;
Hasten to me, O God!
You are my help and my protector;
O Yahweh, do not delay.

71.3:
Be to me a rock of habitation to which I may continually come;
You have given the command to save me,
For You are my rock and my fortress.

71.6:
By You I have been sustained from my birth;
You are He who took me from my mother’s womb;
My praise is continually of You.

71.15:
My mouth shall recount Your righteousness
And Your salvation all day long;
For I do not know the sum of them.

71.19:
For Your righteousness, O God, reaches to the heavens,
You who have done great things;
O God, who is like You?

72.15:
So may he live! And may they give to him the gold of Sheba;
And let each pray for him continually;
Let each bless him all day long.

72.16:
May there be abundance of grain in the earth on top of the mountains;
May its fruit wave like the cedars of Lebanon;
And may those from the city blossom like vegetation of the earth.

72.17:
May his name endure forever;
May his name increase as long as the sun shines;
Let all nations be blessed in him;
Let all nations call him blessed.

72.19:
And blessed be His glorious name forever;
And may the whole earth be filled with His glory.
Amen, and Amen.

73.28:
But as for me, the nearness of God is my good;
I have set Lord Yahweh as my refuge,
That I may recount all Your works.

74.2:
Remember Your congregation, which You have purchased of old,
Which You have redeemed to be the tribe of Your inheritance;
And this Mount Zion, where You have dwelt.

74.9:
We do not see our signs;
There is no longer any prophet,
Nor is there any among us who knows how long.

75.1:
We give thanks to You, O God, we give thanks,
For Your name is near;
Men recount Your wondrous deeds.

75.8:
For a cup is in the hand of Yahweh, and the wine foams;
It is full of His mixture, and He pours from this;
Surely all the wicked of the earth must drain and drink down its dregs.

76.5:
The stouthearted were plundered,
They sank into sleep;
And none of the warriors could use his hands.

77.2:
In the day of my distress I sought the Lord;
In the night my hand was stretched out without weariness;
My soul refused to be comforted.

77.6:
I remember my music in the night;
I am musing with my heart,
And my spirit is searching:

77.16:
The waters saw You, O God;
The waters saw You, they were in anguish;
The deeps also trembled.

77.17:
The clouds poured out water;
The skies gave forth a sound;
Your arrows went here and there.

77.18:
The sound of Your thunder was in the whirlwind;
The lightnings lit up the world;
The earth trembled and shook.

78.21:
Therefore Yahweh heard and was full of wrath;
And a fire was kindled against Jacob
And anger also mounted against Israel,

78.38:
But He, being compassionate, atoned for their iniquity and did not destroy them;
And He abounded in turning back His anger
And did not arouse all His wrath.

78.50:
He leveled a path for His anger;
He did not hold back their soul from death,
But gave over their life to the plague,

79.1:
O God, the nations have come into Your inheritance;
They have defiled Your holy temple;
They have laid Jerusalem in ruins.

79.8:
Do not remember our former iniquities against us;
Let Your compassion quickly approach us,
For we are brought very low.

79.13:
But as for us, as Your people and the sheep of Your pasture,
We will give thanks to You forever;
From generation to generation we will recount Your praise.

80.1:
O Shepherd of Israel, give ear,
You who guide Joseph like a flock;
You who are enthroned above the cherubim, shine forth!

81.7:
You called in distress and I rescued you;
I answered you in the hiding place of thunder;
I tested you at the waters of Meribah. Selah.

81.10:
I am Yahweh your God,
Who brought you up from the land of Egypt;
Open your mouth wide and I will fill it.

82.5:
They do not know and do not understand;
They walk about in darkness;
All the foundations of the earth are shaken.

84.11:
For Yahweh God is a sun and shield;
Yahweh gives grace and glory;
No good thing does He withhold from those who walk blamelessly.

85.8:
Let me hear what the God, Yahweh, will speak;
For He will speak peace to His people, to His holy ones;
But let them not turn back to folly.

86.11:
Teach me Your way, O Yahweh;
I will walk in Your truth;
Unite my heart to fear Your name.

86.16:
Turn to me, and be gracious to me;
Oh grant Your strength to Your slave,
And save the son of Your maidservant.

87.4:
“I shall mention Rahab and Babylon among those who know Me;
Behold, Philistia and Tyre with Ethiopia:
‘This one was born there.’”

88.8:
You have removed my acquaintances far from me;
You have set me as an abomination to them;
I am shut up and cannot go out.

88.9:
My eye has wasted away because of affliction;
I have called upon You every day, O Yahweh;
I have spread out my hands to You.

89.19:
Formerly You spoke in vision to Your holy ones,
And said, “I have bestowed help to a mighty one;
I have exalted one chosen from the people.

90.17:
Let the favor of the Lord our God be upon us;
And establish for us the work of our hands;
Establish the work of our hands.

91.4:
He will cover you with His pinions,
And under His wings you will take refuge;
His truth is a large shield and bulwark.

91.15:
He will call upon Me, and I will answer him;
I will be with him in his distress;
I will rescue him and honor him.

92.9:
For, behold, Your enemies, O Yahweh,
For, behold, Your enemies will perish;
All the workers of iniquity will be scattered.

93.1:
Yahweh reigns, He is clothed with majesty;
Yahweh has clothed and girded Himself with strength;
Indeed, the world is established, it will not be shaken.

93.5:
Your testimonies are very faithful;
Holiness befits Your house,
O Yahweh, forevermore.

94.23:
He has brought back their iniquity upon them
And will destroy them in their evil;
Yahweh our God will destroy them.

96.10:
Say among the nations, “Yahweh reigns;
Indeed, the world is established, it will not be shaken;
He will render justice to the peoples with equity.”

97.7:
Let all those be ashamed who serve graven images,
Who boast of idols;
Worship Him, all you gods!

97.10:
Hate evil, you who love Yahweh,
Who keeps the souls of His holy ones;
He delivers them from the hand of the wicked.

98.9:
Before Yahweh, for He is coming to judge the earth;
He will judge the world with righteousness
And the peoples with equity.

99.4:
The strength of the King loves justice;
You have established equity;
You have done justice and righteousness in Jacob.

99.5:
Exalt Yahweh our God
And worship at the footstool of His feet;
Holy is He.

99.6:
Moses and Aaron were among His priests,
And Samuel was among those who called on His name;
They would call upon Yahweh and He would answer them.

99.7:
He would speak to them in the pillar of cloud;
They kept His testimonies
And the statute that He gave them.

99.8:
O Yahweh our God, You answered them;
You were a forgiving God to them,
And yet an avenger of their evil deeds.

100.3:
Know that Yahweh, He is God;
It is He who has made us, and not we ourselves;
We are His people and the sheep of His pasture.

100.5:
For Yahweh is good;
His lovingkindness endures forever
And His faithfulness, generation unto generation.

101.3:
I will set no vile thing before my eyes;
I hate the work of those who fall away;
It shall not cling to me.

102.2:
Do not hide Your face from me in the day of my distress;
Incline Your ear to me;
In the day when I call answer me quickly.

102.26:
Even they will perish, but You will remain;
And all of them will wear out like a garment;
Like clothing You will change them and they will be changed.

103.22:
Bless Yahweh, all you works of His,
In all places of His rule;
Bless Yahweh, O my soul!

104.1:
Bless Yahweh, O my soul!
O Yahweh my God, You are very great;
You are clothed with splendor and majesty,

104.3:
He lays the beams of His upper chambers in the waters;
He sets up the clouds to be His chariot;
He walks upon the wings of the wind;

104.24:
How numerous are Your works, O Yahweh!
In wisdom You have made them all;
The earth is full of Your possessions.

104.29:
You hide Your face, they are dismayed;
You take away their spirit, they breathe their last
And return to their dust.

106.1:
Praise Yah!
Oh give thanks to Yahweh, for He is good;
For His lovingkindness endures forever.

106.7:
Our fathers in Egypt did not consider Your wondrous deeds;
They did not remember Your abundant lovingkindnesses,
But they rebelled by the sea, at the Red Sea.

106.43:
Many times He would deliver them;
But they were rebellious in their counsel,
And so they sank down in their iniquity.

108.8:
Gilead is Mine, Manasseh is Mine;
Ephraim also is the helmet of My head;
Judah is My scepter.

108.9:
Moab is My washbowl;
Over Edom I shall throw My shoe;
Over Philistia I will make a loud shout.”

109.28:
Let them curse, but You bless;
They arise and will be put to shame,
But Your slave shall be glad.

110.3:
Your people will offer themselves freely in the day of Your power;
In the splendor of holiness, from the womb of the dawn,
The dew of Your youthfulness will be Yours.

111.9:
He has sent redemption to His people; 
He has commanded His covenant forever;
Holy and fearsome is His name.

112.9:
He has given freely to the needy, 
His righteousness stands forever;
His horn will be raised in glory.

115.7:
As for their hands, they do not feel;
As for their feet, they do not walk;
They do not make a sound with their throat.

116.3:
The cords of death encompassed me
And the distresses of Sheol found me;
I found distress and sorrow.

118.12:
They surrounded me like bees;
They were extinguished as a fire of thorns;
In the name of Yahweh I will surely cut them off.

119.48:
And I shall lift up my hands to Your commandments,
Which I love;
And I will muse on Your statutes.

127.5:
How blessed is the man who fills his quiver with them;
They will not be ashamed
When they speak with enemies in the gate.

129.8:
And those who pass by will not say,
“The blessing of Yahweh be upon you;
We bless you in the name of Yahweh.”

130.7:
O Israel, wait for Yahweh;
For with Yahweh there is lovingkindness,
And with Him is abundant redemption.

131.1:
O Yahweh, my heart is not exalted, and my eyes are not raised high;
And I do not involve myself in great matters,
Or in matters too marvelous for me.

133.3:
It is like the dew of Hermon
Coming down upon the mountains of Zion;
For there, Yahweh commanded the blessing—life forever.

135.1:
Praise Yah!
Praise the name of Yahweh;
Praise Him, O slaves of Yahweh,

135.7:
The One who causes the clouds to ascend from the end of the earth;
Who makes lightnings for the rain,
Who brings forth the wind from His storehouses.

135.11:
Sihon, king of the Amorites,
And Og, king of Bashan,
And all the kingdoms of Canaan;

138.2:
I will worship toward Your holy temple
And give thanks to Your name for Your lovingkindness and Your truth;
For You have magnified Your word according to all Your name.

138.7:
Though I walk in the midst of distress, You will revive me;
You will stretch forth Your hand against the wrath of my enemies,
And Your right hand will save me.

138.8:
Yahweh will accomplish what concerns me;
O Yahweh, Your lovingkindness endures forever;
Do not fail the works of Your hands.

139.14:
I will give thanks to You, for I am fearfully and wonderfully made;
Wonderful are Your works,
And my soul knows it very well.

139.15:
My frame was not hidden from You,
When I was made in secret,
And intricately woven in the depths of the earth;

140.4:
Keep me, O Yahweh, from the hands of the wicked;
Guard me from violent men
Who give thought to trip up my steps.

140.5:
The proud have hidden a trap for me, and cords;
They have spread a net by the wayside;
They have set snares for me. Selah.

140.10:
May burning coals be shaken out upon them;
May He cause them to fall into the fire,
Into bottomless pits from which they can never rise.

141.5:
Let the righteous smite me in lovingkindness and reprove me;
It is oil upon the head;
Let not my head refuse it,
For still my prayer is against their evil deeds.

142.4:
Look to the right and see;
That there is no one who regards me;
A way of escape has been destroyed from me;
No one cares for my soul.

142.5:
I cried out to You, O Yahweh;
I said, “You are my refuge,
My portion in the land of the living.

143.3:
For the enemy has pursued my soul;
He has crushed my life to the ground;
He has made me inhabit dark places, like those who have long been dead.

143.5:
I remember the days of old;
I meditate on all You have done;
I muse on the work of Your hands.

143.7:
Answer me quickly, O Yahweh, my spirit wastes away;
Do not hide Your face from me,
Or I will become like those who go down to the pit.

143.8:
Cause me to hear Your lovingkindness in the morning;
For I trust in You;
Cause me to know the way in which I should walk;
For to You I lift up my soul.

143.10:
Teach me to do Your will,
For You are my God;
Let Your good Spirit lead me on level ground.

144.1:
Blessed be Yahweh, my rock,
Who trains my hands for war,
My fingers for battle;

144.7:
Send forth Your hand from on high;
Set me free and deliver me out of many waters,
Out of the hand of foreigners

146.6:
Who made heaven and earth,
The sea and all that is in them;
Who keeps truth forever;

146.7:
Who does justice for the oppressed;
Who gives food to the hungry.
Yahweh sets the prisoners free.

146.8:
Yahweh opens the eyes of the blind;
Yahweh raises up those who are bowed down;
Yahweh loves the righteous;

146.9:
Yahweh keeps the sojourners;
He helps up the orphan and the widow,
But He bends the way of the wicked.

147.1:
Praise Yah!
For it is good to sing praises to our God;
For it is pleasant and praise is becoming.

147.20:
He has not done so with any nation;
So as for His judgments, they have not known them.
Praise Yah!

148.1:
Praise Yah!
Praise Yahweh from the heavens;
Praise Him in the heights!

148.13:
Let them praise the name of Yahweh,
For His name alone is set on high;
His splendor is above earth and heaven.

149.9:
To execute on them the judgment written;
This is the majesty of all His holy ones.
Praise Yah!

150.1:
Praise Yah!
Praise God in His sanctuary;
Praise Him in His mighty expanse.
